\newlabel{tab:ppci}{{7}{5}{Method comparison under DGP~C (both covariate and outcome errors), $K{=}2$, extreme regime, $n_{\text {expert}}{=}250$, 100 MC runs. EC-HTE+PPCI achieves near-zero bias with lower RMSE than either component alone. DSL per-subgroup has comparable bias but 15--25\% higher RMSE due to lack of cross-subgroup shrinkage}{table.caption.10}{}}
